From 05a4bd76fc61696377aa31a7d45dbdc24cac9dfb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: miroe <260228444+boartat@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 13:04:27 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] mullion: MUMA v2 - reclaim spares of dynamic resources (port
 from DXMT)

The spare allocations a WRITE_DISCARD renames away are kept in each dynamic
resource's queue for reuse and were never freed: after a burst, the memory
stays allocated for the rest of the process (DXMT #260, the same in
Mullion). This ports miroe's MUMA v2 from DXMT (patches/dxmt/0001-0003 in
the Miro repository):
- a registry per command queue and a thread that trims every 250 ms,
  independent of submissions: a spare the GPU is done with is freed after
  2 s; past an idle limit of min(1 GB, budget / 8) or over the budget,
  idle spares are freed whatever their age, and before a new large
  allocation that would pass the budget (policy after DXVK's allocator,
  src/dxvk/dxvk_memory.cpp, zlib; no DXVK code copied);
- large Metal-allocated spares are purgeable while idle
  (MTLResource_setPurgeableState, WMTUnixResourceSetPurgeableState);
- dynamic linear textures take part too.

What differs from the DXMT version, for Mullion:
- the budget is Mullion's memory::Budget (95% of the working set, lower
  under macOS memory pressure) instead of the working set minus 1%;
- an allocation may hold several names (Mullion's doubling within a
  staging block), so a spare counts its own bytes;
- a purgeable spare leaves the residency heartbeat's set and rejoins it
  when reused: kept in the set, the heartbeat's requestResidency keeps it
  resident and purgeable spares save nothing (measured: 923 MB with,
  308 MB without, spares kept 60 s; MIROE_MUMA_KEEP_HEARTBEAT=1);
- the trim thread starts once the registry knows the device.

ARM64 Wine + FEX, M4 Pro, macOS 27.2, Engine/tests/c (GPU memory after
the burst): buffers 923 -> 308 MB, an application that stops submitting
923 -> 308 MB, 64 MB dynamic textures 971 -> 199 MB, reused data verified.
Game-like test, 3 runs: after the first fight 584 -> 303 MB, in the menu
629 -> 294 MB; fight frame times within run spread (fight2 p99 9.83 ->
8.19 ms). Small discards, 5 interleaved runs: 3.117 -> 3.136 ms/frame
(ranges 3.067-3.159 and 3.064-3.219: no measurable difference).

Source: miroe (Miro project). License: LGPL-2.1-or-later, like Mullion.
Written with AI assistance and reviewed by measurement; not submitted.
